\title{plancap: plan-enabled development capacity from planning rules and parcels}
\description{
plancap estimates the floorspace and dwellings that planning rules enable
on each land parcel. It is written to be independent of any one
jurisdiction: the rules are data (a \emph{rulebook}), not code.
}
\section{Scope}{

Results are \strong{plan-enabled, gross, blank-slate} capacity: what the rules
would allow if no buildings existed. They are not estimates of feasible,
infrastructure-ready or likely development.
}

\section{Example data}{

\code{\link[=exampleton]{exampleton()}} loads a synthetic town built to exercise every rule type.
It is deliberately placed offshore so it cannot be mistaken for a real
place.
